    <briefdescription>
<para>A proxy object for computing a pointer via indirecting a copy of a reference. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This is used in APIs which need to produce a pointer but for which the reference might be a temporary. The proxy preserves the reference internally and exposes the pointer via a arrow operator. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
